sketch-orca oracle patch 0001: the clock knob, SKETCH_ORCA_ORACLE_TIME.
Modified for Sketch, 2026-11-06.

With SKETCH_ORCA_ORACLE_TIME set to a time in whole seconds since 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC, from
315532800 (1980-01-01, the first time a zip entry's DOS date holds) to 4102444799 (2099-12-31
23:59:59), the oracle reads that time, as UTC, wherever the engine reads the clock into what it
writes:
- the time and the local time behind Utils::local_timestamp (GCode.cpp:2576, the G-code header's
  "generated by ... on" line): get_current_time_utc and time2str (Time.cpp), whose local time is
  then UTC;
- PlaceholderParser::update_timestamp (PlaceholderParser.cpp:78-100): the timestamp, year, month,
  day, hour, minute and second placeholders;
- the time of every entry miniz writes into a 3MF (miniz.c, mz_zip_writer_add_mem_ex_v2,
  mz_zip_writer_add_read_buf_callback and mz_zip_writer_add_staged_open), whatever time the caller
  gives: mz_zip_writer_add_file_ex gives the source file's modification time, which is the clock
  when the engine wrote that file (the plate's G-code) in this run. miniz, which is C, reads the
  knob itself, through sketch_orca_oracle_clock.c;
- the srand(time(NULL)) of Fill/Lightning/Generator.cpp:34, which is seeded with the pinned time;
- FilamentGroup's time budget (FlushTimeMachine), which then reads no time passed, so its search
  ends by its own count only;
- the backup folder's name (Model::get_backup_path) and the import time PresetBundle records.
The 3MF CreationDate and ModificationDate are written empty by OrcaSlicer 2.4.2
(bbs_3mf.cpp:6835-6836), so no clock reaches them. A value that is not such a time stops the
oracle before it does anything else, with exit code 78. Unset, nothing changes.

